The batch conv of the gated delta net: the precision modes and the packed path (lab proposal)

GDN_CONV_CHUNK is the largest op of a 512-token prefill of the 4B (27 % of the DSP time, 1.27
instructions per packet). Its hot loop is one chain of about 70 dependent qfloat operations for
each 32 channels. On the v79 a packet costs 2 cycles, and a multiply result is ready 2 packets
later, thus one chain waits at each step and leaves the packets almost empty.

gdn_conv_f16_mode selects the path, and tools/htp-lab (target gdn_chunk, --f16 N) measures the
cycles and the error of each against a scalar reference. Mode 0 is the code of the checkout.
Modes 1 to 3 keep the chain and change the precision only. Mode 4 is the packed path: 4 token
rows in each iteration as independent chains, f16 taps with a 32-bit accumulator, and the int16
SiLU of hvx-silu-i16.h (2 int16 multiplies fit one packet, 1 qfloat multiply does).

