+// The precision of the batch conv. The taps are 4 products, thus the accumulator choice is cheap to
+// measure, and tools/htp-lab (target gdn_chunk, --f16 N) reports the cycles and the error of each.
+//   0  f32 taps, f32 accumulate, f32 SiLU (the reference path)
+//   1  f32 taps, f32 accumulate, f16 SiLU
+//   2  f16 taps, 32-bit accumulate, f16 SiLU. The f16 multiply of the HVX is a widening multiply,
+//      its products are qf32, thus the wide accumulator needs no conversion.
+//   3  f16 taps, f16 accumulate, f16 SiLU. Every product goes back to f16 before the sum.
+//   4  the packed path: f16 taps, 32-bit accumulate, int16 SiLU, 4 token rows in each iteration.
